      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T14:08:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practice, the PDOs at higher indexes have higher voltages.  Changing this to `mv \u003e\u003d highest_mw` will select the higher voltage PDO at the same wattage.\nAlternatively, we can just explicitly pick the higher voltage.\n\n```\nif (mw \u003e highest_mw ||\n    (mw \u003d\u003d highest_mw \u0026\u0026 mv \u003e selected_mv))\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1958,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1958,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a4221a059af5cf0d6696e74988a6baaa06d505dc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95f76ff7_3c01a612",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1958,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T17:39:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In TCPMv2, we explicitly have voltage preference as an optional [feature](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usb_pd_dual_role.c;l\u003d114;drc\u003d2c108f019bf13230b6c6ee289cd312e8980dddac). To the extent possible, we should probably conform these implementations.",
      "parentUuid": "1b933afa_a0ed2015",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1958,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1958,
        "endChar": 24
      },
