        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T17:39:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: IDK if this is worth it, but as long as you\u0027re refactoring, if `pdo` were a `uint32_t *`, that one value could be used to get both the PDO contents and their index. That would remove the possibility of these fields being inconsistent, at the possible expense of making accesses to the remaining field less direct. It might also make `pdo` not-to-be-trusted during the time between the Source sending new Source Caps and us sending a new Request, but I think that was probably already the case.",
      "revId": "a4221a059af5cf0d6696e74988a6baaa06d505dc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
